# Git already stores every text file in this repo with LF endings. Check them
# out that way on every platform, rather than letting core.autocrlf rewrite them
# per-machine.
#
# This is load-bearing, not tidiness. dist/ is committed and CI re-builds it to
# check it is current. esbuild inlines the sources it bundled into
# dist/client/app.js.map and JSON-escapes their newlines, so building from a
# CRLF working tree bakes literal "\r\n" into that map. Being escaped text
# rather than real line endings, git's own eol conversion can never normalize
# it, so a Windows build and a Linux build commit genuinely different bytes and
# the dist/ freshness check fails for whoever pushed second.
* text=auto eol=lf
